      "title": "The postcard that made Krampus",
      "headline": "THE POSTCARD THAT MADE KRAMPUS",
      "text": "The Krampus most people picture today owes a great deal to the postcard. In 1869, Austria-Hungary introduced what is often called the world's first official postcard. Within decades, Krampus appeared on many colorful cards: dark fur, horns, a long red tongue, and chains.",
